   "id": "wlkNg_Jcd5oJ",
   "from": "Ed Kademan",
   "author": "cde2961f2a305c8a",
   "date": "2011-04-19T15:19:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: problem with time scale and cut.default",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "John Rauser &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jra...@gmail.com</a>&gt; writes:<p></p>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<p>&gt; You might try specifying a timezone when creating your data.  I have<br>&gt; experienced a similar problem and can work around it by specifying a<br>&gt; timezone as in: <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/925852\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/925852&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792379816908000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2E02lv6KGPzKGP-Gjr9sJx\">https://gist.github.com/925852</a><br>&gt;<br>&gt; -J<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; On Mon, Apr 18, 2011 at 7:58 AM, Ed Kademan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">edm...@kademan.org</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;&gt; Hi,<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; I am trying to do a time series plot using a data frame d with `Time&#39;<br>&gt;&gt; and `Value&#39; columns but am getting an error:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;  &gt; li &lt;- geom_line(aes(x=Time, y=Value))<br>&gt;&gt;  &gt; ggplot(d) + li<br>&gt;&gt;  Error in cut.default(unclass(x), unclass(breaks), labels = labels,<br>&gt;&gt;    right = right, : cannot allocate vector of length 1293858001<br>&gt;&gt;<br></p>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p>&gt;&gt; ...<p>Thank you for the tip.  You are right, the problem is timezone related,<br>but I can&#39;t seem to reliably fix it by explicitly specifying the time<br>zone in my data.  For the time being what works for me is to slightly<br>modify R&#39;s `cut.POSIXt&#39; function as follows:<p>--8&lt;---------------cut here---------------start-------------&gt;8---<br>ejk@dl:~/R$ diff -c ejk*<br>*** ejk.cut.POSIXt-orig.R\t2011-04-19 10:31:41.000000000 -0400<br>--- ejk.cut.POSIXt.R\t2011-04-19 10:18:32.000000000 -0400<br>***************<br>*** 60,65 ****<br>--- 60,66 ----<br>              end &lt;- as.POSIXlt(end + (366 * step * 86400))<br>              end$mon &lt;- 0L<br>              end$mday &lt;- 1L<br>+             end$isdst &lt;- -1L<br>              breaks &lt;- seq(start, end, breaks)<br>          }<br>          else if (valid == 9L) {<br>--8&lt;---------------cut here---------------end---------------&gt;8---<p>and use that.  If I truly get to the bottom of this I will post more.<p>EdK<br></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
